 and emergency readiness.\n\nReview when needed Come back before starting solids, before travel, or when your baby becomes more mobile.\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\nA few details about what is included, how online infant CPR education works, when to start, and how families use Infant Safety & CPR for choking response, safe sleep, car seats, babyproofing, and emergency readiness.\n\nWhat is included in Infant Safety & CPR?\n\nInfant Safety & CPR gives you practical online parent education for baby safety, including infant CPR, choking response, breathing emergencies, safe sleep, crib safety, car seat basics, baby gear safety, feeding safety, medication safety, water safety, fire safety, babyproofing, first aid kits, and emergency planning.\n\nThe goal is not to scare you. It is to help you understand what to do, what to watch for, and how to feel more prepared if something happens.\n\nWill I get certified in infant CPR after taking this course?\n\nNo. This course teaches life-saving skills and safety education, but it is not an official CPR certification course.\n\nFor CPR certification, you need hands-on skills testing with a certified instructor. This course is designed to help parents and caregivers learn the concepts, see clear demonstrations, practice at home, and feel more prepared in an emergency.\n\nDoes this replace my pediatrician or emergency care?\n\nNo. This course is online parent education. It does not replace medical care, emergency care, an individualized safety evaluation, or an in-person CPR certification course.\n\nFor urgent health or safety concerns, call 911 or seek emergency care. For medical questions about your baby, contact your pediatrician or healthcare provider.\n\nHow long do I have access?\n\nYou get 12 months of unlimited access to Infant Safety & CPR.\n\nThat gives you time to learn before baby arrives, revisit lessons as your baby grows, and review key skills with your partner or caregivers when safety questions come up.\n\nDo I have to watch everything in order?\n\nNo. You can watch the course in order, or you can use it like a baby safety library and jump to the topic you need most.\n\nMany families start with infant CPR, choking response, and safe sleep, then return later for car seats, babyproofing, water safety, medication safety, and emergency planning.\n\nIs Infant Safety & CPR HSA/FSA eligible?\n\nYes. You will receive a receipt that you can submit to your HSA or FSA plan administrator.\n\nPlan rules can vary, so we recommend checking with your individual plan if you have questions about reimbursement.\n\nDo you offer a money-back guarantee?\n\nYes. We offer a 15-day money-back guarantee.\n\nIf the course is not the right fit, reach out to our team within 15 days of purchase. We want you to feel comfortable getting started.\n\nDo you offer financial assistance?\n\nYes. We offer reduced-cost options for families who need financial assistance, and your healthcare provider may also be able to help cover the cost.\n\nBecause our courses require time, resources, and ongoing support to provide, we do ask each family to make an investment when they are able.\n\nIf you are in need, please reach out to our team directly at help@nurturednest.org. In your message, please include:\n\n  * The course you are interested in\n  * Your baby’s age or due date\n  * The best email address to register you with\n  * The amount you are able to invest at this time\n\nOur team will review your message and do our best to help.\n\nStill wondering if this is the right fit? Visit our full FAQ page, send your specific question to help@nurturednest.org, or browse our free parent education blog to get a feel for how we teach.\n\nReady when you are\n\n## You may never need these skills.\nBut knowing them can change everything.\n\nInfant Safety & CPR gives you clear, practical guidance for choking response, infant CPR, safe sleep, car seat basics, babyproofing, emergency planning, and the everyday safety questions 